 "text": "Auditor's Office / Newton County, Indiana\nSkip over navigation\nNewton County\nThe Official Government Website for Newton County, Indiana\nDocuments | Site Tools\nSearch\nSearch Submit\nStart Content\nToggle Menu\nHome\nAbout Community Events\nCounty Demographics\nDocument Center\nEmployment Opportunities\nEvents Calendar\nResident Information\nCourthouse Assessor\nAuditor\nClerk\nCourts\nProbation\nProsecutor\nRecorder\nTreasurer\nCourthouse Directory\nGovernment Center Adult Education\nBuilding Department\nCoroner's Office\nCounty Commissioners Commissioners Meeting Schedule\nMeet Your Commissioners\nCounty Council Council Meeting Schedule\nMeet Your Council Members\nHealth Department\nPark Board\nPurdue Extension\nRecycling\nSoil & Water Conservation District\nVeteran's Service Officer\nWIC\nWorkOne\nCounty Facilities Ambulance Service\nAnimal Control\nCommunications Center\nDepartment Child Services\nDivision of Family Resources\nEmergency Management Agency\nHighway Department\nMaintenace Department\nMap of County Offices\nSearch Locations by Name\nSurveyor's Office\nSheriff Dept In Remembrance\nNewton County Jail\nContact Ask a Question\nBoards & Commissions Board of Zoning Appeals\nDrainage Board\nPlan Commission\nPlat Commission\nCounty Departments A-G Ambulance Services\nAnimal Control\nAssessor's Office\nAuditor's Office\nBuilding Department\nClerk of Courts\nCoroner's Office\nEconomic Development\nElections & Voting\nEmergency Management Agency\nEmergency Medical Services\nGIS Services\nCounty Departments H-Z Health Department\nHighway Department\nMaintenance Department\nNewton County Extension Office\nProbation Department\nProsecutor's Office\nRecorder's Office\nRecycling\nSheriff's Department\nSoil & Water Conservation District\nSurveyor's Office\nTreasurer's Office\nZoning\nVeteran's Service Officer\nSubmit an Online Form\nView the County Staff Directory\nEmployee Resources Doculivery\nEmployee Webmail\nEmployment Application\nYou are here: Home » Officials » Auditor's Office\nAuditor's Office\nIn order to emphasize the seemingly endless responsibilities, which rest with the County Auditors and their staff, we have prepared a list of duties for each area of our Department. The duties range from simple ministerial tasks such as keeping minutes of the various Board meetings for which we serve as secretary, to the highly technical duties of financial statement preparation and compliance with federal tax guidelines and programs.\nThe office of County Auditor has evolved dramatically from a bookkeeper and part-time secretary to a financial manager whose responsibilities impact the financial well-being of county government.\nClick here for more information on Staff Duties.\nProperty Tax Deduction Forms:\n-Homestead Deduction Form\n-Over 65 Credit Form\n-Blind/Disabled Credit Form\n-Disabled Veterans Deduction\n-Heritage Barn Deduction Form\nNews\nUseful Links\nServices\nNews & Notices\n2026 Tax Reform Letter\nUseful Links\nOver 65 Credit Form | Heritage Barn Deduction Form | Geothermal, Solar Energy system or Solar, Wind, or Hydroelectric Deduction Form |\nDisabled Veterans Deduction | Blind/Disabled Deduction form | Political Subdivision Dashboard |\nCircuit Breaker Caps Fact Sheet | TS-1 Information Packet | Homestead Verification Form Fact Sheet |\nServices\nContact Your Local DLGF Officials | Pay Property Taxes Online | Search for My Tax Information |\nTax Payer Calculators | | |\nContact Us\nAuditor's Office\n201 N 3rd St\nKentland, IN 47951\nGet Directions\n|\nLocation/Facility Details\nPhone: (888) 663-9866 x 1200\nFax: (219) 474-9245\nEmail Us\nStaff Directory\nOffice Hours:\nMonday-Friday 8:00 a.m.-4:00 p.m.\nIn this Department\nStaff Duties\nTopics of Interest\nProperty Tax Deductions\nTax Payer Calculators\nTax Sale Rules\nUnderstanding My Tax Bill\nMore Information\nDocument Center News\nUseful Links\nForms & Applications\nMinutes\nServices Index\nSite Design and Content Copyright © 2026 Newton Co